# Database snapshots. THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC.
#
# `node scripts/backup-db.js` defaults to ./backups, so running it from
# store-app/server/ drops a directory of customer names, phone numbers and
# order history into the working tree, where `git add -A` will happily take it.
# Publishing that is not a mistake you can take back: a public repo cannot be
# un-published, the blob survives a history rewrite on GitHub's side, and any
# fork keeps a copy.
#
# .githooks/pre-commit and CI's no-snapshots job block these paths as well,
# because a gitignore is only advice, `git add -f` walks straight past it.
backups/
*.ndjson
*.ndjson.gz
